bpftune (0.4.16) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix: heal poisoned bucket references.  When a socket's min_rtt
    is more than REF_HEAL_FACTOR times the current reference (or its
    rate is more than REF_HEAL_FACTOR below the ceiling), move the
    reference 1/REF_HEAL_DIV of the gap toward the observed value.
    Prevents a single fast socket that hit an empty bucket first from
    permanently capping the RTT term for all subsequent traffic.
    Healthy traffic never triggers this.  Parameters: factor 3, div 16.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:05:28 +0200

bpftune (0.4.15) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix: reject bucket-reference updates that are more than 2x better
    than the current reference.  A single anomalous socket (e.g. a
    fast CDN hitting the same gateway as a 30ms tunnel) had been
    able to permanently anchor min_rtt far below real traffic and
    saturate rtt_term at its cap.  Also guard rate_term against
    negative when a socket exceeds the ceiling without updating it.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:25:56 +0200

bpftune (0.4.14) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix: change RTT term to measure queueing delay (avg_rtt - bucket
    min_rtt) instead of min-against-min, which was path-constant and
    carried no algorithm signal on stable paths. Adds avg_rtt parameter
    to tcp_metric_calc, sourced from tp->srtt_us >> 3.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:42:03 +0200

bpftune (0.4.13) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix: pass current socket's rate_delivered to tcp_metric_calc
    instead of the algorithm's all-time-best rate. Previously the
    rate term was frozen per algorithm (only changed when the alg
    set a new personal best), making half the metric historic while
    the RTT half was live per-socket.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:09:38 +0200

bpftune (0.4.12) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix: only sockets with >= METRIC_MIN_SEGS total segments update
    the per-algorithm metric and bucket references. Prevents small
    control sockets from pinning the bucket min_rtt to an unachievable
    floor, which had caused every real connection to saturate the RTT
    term and lock the tuner onto whichever algorithm got the poisoned
    bucket first.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:54:55 +0200

